Translator&#8217;s Summary

This halacha is built on Likutay Moharan I:13 (&ldquo;Happy Is the People &mdash; Providence&rdquo;), one of Rabainu&rsquo;s most intricate teachings, which establishes that complete Divine Providence (Hashgachah) comes through receiving Torah, which comes through gathering souls, which comes through breaking the craving for money via tz&rsquo;dakah. Reb Nosson maps the entire Pesach&ndash;S&rsquo;firah&ndash;Shavuos arc onto this chain: Pesach = Avraham / chesed / tz&rsquo;dakah / matzah = breaking the craving for money. The omer of barley = &ldquo;I have gathered my myrrh with my spice&rdquo; = gathering both the bitter souls (fallen desires = animal food) and the good souls. The S&rsquo;firah = bringing scattered souls under the count so that not one is lost. Shavuos = Atzeres (Assembly) = all souls finally gathered = Torah received = complete Hashgachah. The Shavuos customs are decoded: staying awake all night = the &ldquo;Eye that does not slumber&rdquo; = breaking the &ldquo;sleep&rdquo; of the craving for money. Eating dairy = &ldquo;His eyes bathing in milk&rdquo; = the eyes of Providence receiving from the open Eye. Reading Rus = revelation of Mashiach / David&rsquo;s kingship. David&rsquo;s passing on Shavuos = the sun setting as the new sun of Mashiach rises. The stunning wordplay: &ldquo;when he places his eye in the cup (bakos)&rdquo; / &ldquo;in the purse (bakis)&rdquo; = the craving for money blemishes wine (= the bloods) which blemishes the eyes (= Providence). And: &ldquo;silver refined, purified seven times&rdquo; = the 7&times;7 weeks of S&rsquo;firah purifying the &ldquo;silver&rdquo; of the craving for money, extracting the sparks, and making from them Torah. Pesach: Avraham / Chesed / Matzah = Tz&rsquo;dakah &rarr; break the craving for money
